  era: "10th\u201313th c. CE \xB7 Section 12 \xB7 Early Medieval India \xB7 c. 700 \u2013 1200 CE"
  title: Temple architecture
  text: 'Temple styles matured: the Nagara style of the north, with curved towers, as at Khajuraho and Konark; the Dravida style of the south, with pyramidal towers and gateway gopurams; and the Vesara style of the Deccan, which blends the two.'
